  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.0.1075\n- Added support for hardware-accelerated thick lines (LineThickness > 1). IsLineThicknessInWorldSpace, DepthBias and lines with patterns are also supported. LineCaps (lines with arrows and other ending shapes) and connected lines (miter or beveled line joints) are not supported yet.\n- Implemented PixelsNode and PixelsMaterial.\n- Implemented rendering PhysicallyBasedMaterial (PBR), including support for environment mapping.\n- Implemented rendering per-vertex colored models by using VertexColorMaterial or setting VertexColors data to a mesh.\n- Added ModelMover, ModelRotator and ModelScalar that can be used to move, rotate and scale the selected 3D models.\n- Added TwoDimensionalCamera that can be used to show 2D shapes and lines. The TwoDimensionalCamera class is provided with full source code.\n- Added MultiMaterialModelNode that can show one mesh with different materials. For example, it is used to show a skybox.\n- Implemented importing keyframe and skeletal animations from glTF files. Note that when running in a Debug or Release build, skeletal animation can be very slow. Start the app in Deploy build to run it at full speed.\n- Added support for background and overlay object and line rendering. This is achived by setting ClearDepthStencilBufferBeforeRendering or ClearDepthStencilBufferAfterRendering property on RenderingLayer to true and adding SceneNode to that RenderingLayer. See new Advanced/BackgroundAndOverlayRenderingSample for more info.\n- Fixed glTFImporter when an embedded texture is used by multiple models.\n- Fixed using CustomRenderingLayer for line SceneNodes.\n- And most of changed in the Ab4d.SharpEngine library.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "summary": "Ab4d.SharpEngine.WebGL is a .Net library for 3D rendering in the browser and can be used in Blazor and any other web framework.",
